            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These cookies were very good, I prefer a more cake like oatmeal cookie and these were kind of flat and crispy. Next time I would use less butter as they were a little greasy, but over all very tasty"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Paty"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My mother made these cookies my whole life. Now that she's gone, I continue to make them for family, friends, and most importantly, my dad. I left my recipe a home so I found this recipe and it's exactly like the original one in the black old Good Housekeeping cookbook. I love hem!",
            "datePublished": "2024-09-10T21:53:56.755Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "a1semisweet"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great crispy cookie. This is a traditional cookie recipe. Did not add the cinnamon. Just prefer it without it. Different oils will change the texture of the cookie. Some may want to add a little salt, I did not. Pick another recipe if you want a soft cookie.",
            "datePublished": "2012-10-24T10:52:26.967Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "leslie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I really enjoyed these cookies. I did make one change though. I always taste the cookie dough before baking and thought it was a bit bland so I added 1/2 tsp. salt. I think if you used butter or margarine you wouldn't need to add salt.",
            "datePublished": "2011-07-11T10:36:10.653Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Suzanne M"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These were okay. I thought they were too sweet and they didn't spread out like I thought they would. The dough was a bit dry, but I just used a scoop and it worked pretty well.",
            "datePublished": "2010-11-10T10:52:05.357Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Heather de Vega"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These are really good, but are more like a sugar cookie than a traditional oatmeal cookie. I liked them, but still prefer the traditional, more cake-like oatmeal cookies. I also added half a cup of flaked coconut to this recipe and it made them extra yummy.",
            "datePublished": "2008-10-20T20:10:10.810Z"
          },
          {
